152288556,-5.722029527532868e-06,0.0,-2.455681169521995e-05,-2.610649426060263e-05,-0.4159572720527649,-2.03141188621521,-2.0265558760002023e-06,0.0,-0.00015233787416946143,-2.50339189733495e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,6785,6672,1948,279,12196,323,279,3245,4462,315,279,738,57960,2359,59,35702,37018,90,18,15170,22,2137,59,37018,90,19,15170,18,2137,59,37018,90,16,16,15170,23,2137,59,37018,90,21,15170,16,21,11035,1291,59,31716,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$? Express your answer in simplest form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b66c68e10386bc998e7bacea58bdd9adda26162dc40dd86f60c5b08dfe974b9e"},"seconds":23.111198902130127,"seed":234070600971076160,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to compare the fractions. To make the comparison easier, we'll convert all the fractions to have a common denominator or convert them to decimal form.\n\nFirst, simplify $\\frac{6}{16}$:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{6 \\div 2}{16 \\div 2} = \\frac{3}{8}\n\\]\n\nNow the set is $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{3}{8}\\right\\}$.\n\nWe can compare these fractions by converting them to decimal form:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\n\\]\n\nFrom these decimal values, it is clear that the greatest fraction is $\\frac{11}{8}$ and the least fraction is $\\frac{3}{8}$. Now we need to find the positive difference between these two fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\boxed{1}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to compare the fractions. To make the comparison easier, we'll convert all the fractions to have a common denominator or convert them to decimal form.\n\nFirst, simplify $\\frac{6}{16}$:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{6 \\div 2}{16 \\div 2} = \\frac{3}{8}\n\\]\n\nNow the set is $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{3}{8}\\right\\}$.\n\nWe can compare these fractions by converting them to decimal form:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\n\\]\n\nFrom these decimal values, it is clear that the greatest fraction is $\\frac{11}{8}$ and the least fraction is $\\frac{3}{8}$. Now we need to find the positive difference between these two fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\boxed{1}.","id":"prealgebra:855"}
